WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:11.120
Like many international organizations, the&nbsp;
International Criminal Court is great in theory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:16.800
but a failure in practice. It was formally&nbsp;
founded in 2002 with the admirable goal of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:23.040
ending war crimes, crimes against humanity,&nbsp;
aggression, and genocide. But it has not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:29.520
accomplished its mission. In theory, the ICC an&nbsp;
independent legal institution above politics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.680
In practice, its political agenda devotes&nbsp;
unequal attention to America, Israel, and African&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:42.480
nations. In theory, the ICC only steps in where&nbsp;
national courts aren't fit to investigate crimes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.760
In practice, the ICC targets US soldiers&nbsp;
who've already been tried in American courts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:55.040
yet it ignores the grave human rights violations&nbsp;
committed by Venezuela, China, and Russia. In less&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:00.720
than 20 years, more than 2 billion dollars have&nbsp;
been spent with only nine successful convictions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.880
all against African nations. The ICC's silence&nbsp;
is a betrayal to millions living under tyranny.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.000
Do you think the ICC needs&nbsp;
reform? Let us know in our poll.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.040
Also let us know what other topics you'd&nbsp;
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:22.400
and be sure to like and subscribe for&nbsp;
more research and videos from AEI.

